Key Elements and Terms of the Service Contract
Service Provider: The service provider is <provider>, registered at <Address1>, contactable via <Num1>.
Client: The client is <client>, registered at <Address2>, contactable via <Num2>.
Service Description: The provider agrees to perform <serviceType> services for the client in exchange for <serviceFee> as compensation.
Completion Deadline: The service must be completed by <completionDate>, with confirmation required by <confirmDate>.

Service Provider' s Rights and Obligations
Obligation to deliverService: The provider shall complete the service as agreed by <completionDate>, and notify the client upon completion.
Obligation to correctIssues: If the client raises concerns about the service quality before <confirmDate>, the provider shall make reasonable corrections.
Right to receivePayment: The provider is entitled to receive <serviceFee> upon service completion and client confirmation.
Client' s Rights and Obligations
Obligation to payDeposit: The client shall pay <0.3 * serviceFee> as a deposit upon contract signing.
Obligation to confirmCompletion: Upon receiving notice of service completion, the client shall confirm the service status by <confirmDate>.
Obligation to makePayment: After confirming completion, the client shall pay <0.7 * serviceFee> to the provider.
Right to requestRefund: If the provider fails to complete the service by <completionDate>, the client has the right to request a refund of <0.3 * serviceFee>.

